  "complete_requirement_coverage": false,
  "scope": "Exact captured RGB stacks now replay as rgb_contrast_stack native portable operations and session batches. A singleton explicit ActiveSelection Positions target identifies the active processor while execution maps the entire current TCZ stack; it requires empty free parameters, complete original, in-place plane execution, no unused ranges/calibration/filter overrides. The original is completely validated and retained unchanged before rebinding saved mappings to destination selection and the authored anchor. Destination T/C/Z, crosshair, zoom and pan survive paired publication. Shared exact processor membership produces sample-free metadata descriptors after conservative admission; descriptor sample acquisition throws, invalid later intent/storage/anchor/limits fails before prefix samples, and empty enabled stack steps retain Change::All dependencies without reads/history. All 5292 unchanged actual ImageJ 1.54r stack reference rows pass portable record/JSON roundtrip, explicit original-anchor replay after destination navigation changes, complete stack hashes, geometry, one paired Undo/Redo and immutable original assertions. Fifteen ambiguous-intent cases, five late/preflight cases, four stale revisions, three cancellation/callback cases, one disabled incompatible anchor and two scientific session batches pass. Actual shared workflow widgets load a plain complete capture, edit active Z, keep/reopen a portable program, preview/Apply promoted active pixels and narrowed other-plane pixels, preserve navigation/recorder and perform paired Undo/Redo in standalone C++ and Python launches. Saved mapping choices remain read-only in workflow review. Windows/Linux each pass 22 native suites, three full standalone workflow/batch/RGB UI probes, one installed SDK consumer, ten background repetitions, four hidden GL contexts and 31235 installed Python checks (5323 new), zero failure/error/skip. SDK consumers explicitly retarget the anchor and exercise record/JSON replay, publication and Undo. A failed SDK example include and strict GCC temporary-reference error, plus the Python out-of-range IndexError expectation, were corrected only in test/SDK consumers; final native/production/UI bytes are unchanged and both SDKs pass. Actual source/module origins and 5475 native Linux test/config/fixture files are pinned. One previously unused compiled-source-cache Python UI test matched exact initial Git 0aa3acc bytes; its controlled migration is recorded, while all prior and current Python qualification uses separate SHA-verified native snapshots. Full installed suites use actual disposable venv interpreters. Exact owned scratch is CRC/member-SHA archived before confined removal; final installs, native/SDK probes and useful caches remain. Source/provider caches, frontend copies, phase-local codec work and total RSS remain external to retained-byte estimates. Main brightness/contrast stack controls, stage-choice editing, snapshot/selection/navigation transitions and full G057/ImageJ/Fiji/platform/resource acceptance remain open. Existing scalar/uniform-RGB wire profiles, portable container fields, general registrations, commercial-use inventory and all 99 requirement/status triples remain unchanged. The old Auto producer-source gate remains open.",
